# Notes on backpressure

By the editors, filed under systems.

Every queue is a promise about the future: somebody will drain it.

**Pull quote:** an unbounded queue is a memory leak with good intentions.

Bounding the queue turns a slow consumer into a visible signal instead of an out-of-memory crash at 3 a.m.

Corrections and follow-ups are welcome.
